  "readme_paragraph_proposal": "A sequential 1024-trial CPU/GPU comparison on two fixed g001 paths at -28 dB-Hz completed all four jobs without timeout. Both receiver pairs used the same input hashes and draw seeds; all 4096 score-row vectors per pair had identical winner and admission-gate decisions (CFO maximum absolute score delta 1.74e-07; window 1.44e-05). Correct accepted signal counts were CFO 1298/2048 and Gaussian-window 1288/2048, with zero wrong accepts; each method had zero admissions in 2048 conditional null trials on these paths. Outer CPU/GPU wall times were CFO 105.572/12.110 s (ratio 8.72\u00d7) and window 6.837/6.568 s (ratio 1.04\u00d7); receiver-call times were 98.431/6.096 s and 0.570/0.579 s. For window mode, sampler/UCB consumed 4.801/4.100 s and explicit plan preparation 0.070/0.068 s of those calls. FP32 bulk arithmetic retained FP64 sensitive calibration/evidence stages with TF32 disabled. These are single-run measurements, not universal GPU speedup or false-alarm qualification.",
